message: "Please cite this dated overview when referring to its selected experimental results."
title: "DE10-Nano active noise cancellation: public overview and selected evidence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thomson
    given-names: Neil
version: "2026.11.24"
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pealie/de10-nano-anc-overview"
url: "https://github.com/Pealie/de10-nano-anc-overview"
abstract: "On 24 November 2026, three 60-second matched pairs on three board boots achieved 7.55, 9.03 and 10.14 dB attenuation of the tracked external tone near 200 Hz at the marked RIGHT microphone. All 180 one-second intervals exceeded 3 dB under the phase-ramped source programme. Public I/Q extracts support offline numerical replay. The overview preserves the 21 November abrupt-source benchmark and the 4–5 November experiments."
keywords:
  - active noise cancellation
  - FPGA
  - DE10-Nano
  - digital signal processing
  - adaptive feedback
  - reproducible measurements
